[statement]
Where a name's single candidate states two entries on one name, the first
is the one required: as
`a-sole-candidate-s-dependency-is-required-with-its-constraint`, with `n`
needing `lib>0` before `lib<2`. `lib` is required with `lib>0` and gets
2.0, and `n` cannot be installed beside it; apk refuses. With the entries
the other way round, it installs `lib` 1.0.

[repository]
P:app
V:1
D:so:r

P:r
V:1
p:so:r=1
D:so:n

P:n
V:1
p:so:n=1
D:lib>0 lib<2

P:lib
V:1.0

P:lib
V:2.0

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   lib-2.0:
|     breaks: n-1[lib<2]
|     satisfies: n-1[lib>0]
refused
